  "worked_solution": "To subtract $-6.5$ from $-1.5$, we first combine the two negative signs to make a single plus sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1.5-(-6.5)=-1.5+6.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $-1.5+6.5$, we start at $-1.5$ and move $6$ places to the right. Then, we move another  $0.5$ places to the right.  \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14150464/assets/e327ed5a6489a26d775b83c759c1e8ea21b5584797ce08f1a6e4419c99149392.png)\n\nThus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1.5-(-6.5)=5 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
